and leading space.\n1: /**\n2:  * ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3:  * ║  BREW & BLOOM CAFÉ — CENTRAL CONFIGURATION              ║\n4:  * ║  Edit this file to customise your café platform.        ║\n5:  * ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n6:  */\n7: \n8: const CONFIG = {\n9: \n10:   /* ── CAFÉ IDENTITY ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n11:   cafe: {\n12:     name:        'Brew & Bloom Café',\n13:     tagline:     'Good Coffee. Slow Moments. Beautiful Days.',\n14:     address:     '[Sample Address], Near [Landmark], Haldia, West Bengal – 721657',\n15:     city:        'Haldia, West Bengal',\n16:     phone:       '+91 00000 00000',       // ← Replace with real number\n17:     email:       'hello@brewandbloom.in', // ← Replace with real email\n18:     whatsapp:    '910000000000',          // ← Replace (country code + number, no symbols)\n19:     instagram:   '#',                     // ← Replace with Instagram URL\n20:     facebook:    '#',                     // ← Replace with Facebook URL\n21:   },\n22: \n23:   /* ── RESTAURANT LOCATION ───────────────────────────────── */\n24:   // ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Replace with your actual café GPS coordinates.\n25:   // To find: Google Maps → right-click your location → \"What's here?\"\n26:   restaurant: {\n27:     lat:  22.0667,   // ← Replace: Haldia approximate coordinates\n28:     lng:  88.0686,   // ← Replace: Haldia approximate coordinates\n29:     name: 'Brew & Bloom Café',\n30:     address: '[Sample Address], Haldia, WB',\n31:   },\n32: \n33:   /* ── DELIVERY SETTINGS ─────────────────────────────────── */\n34:   delivery: {\n35:     radiusKm:        10,     // Max delivery radius in km\n36:     baseCharge:      30,     // ₹ base delivery charge\n37:     perKmCharge:     5,      // ₹ per km beyond 3km\n38:     freeAbove:       500,    // ₹ order total for free delivery\n39:     freeRadiusKm:    3,      // km within which delivery is free (if order >= freeAbove)\n40:     minOrderAmount:  100,    // ₹ minimum order\n41:     estimatedMinBase: 30,    // minutes base prep + short delivery\n42:     perKmMinutes:     3,     // additional minutes per km\n43:   },\n44: \n45:   /* ── TAXES ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n46:   tax: {\n47:     gstPercent: 5,   // % GST applied on food subtotal\n48:     // Set to 0 to disable tax display\n49:   },\n50: \n51:   /* ── OPENING HOURS ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n52:   hours: {\n53:     'Mon–Fri': { open: '08:00', close: '21:00' },\n54:     'Saturday': { open: '08:00', close: '22:00' },\n55:     'Sunday':   { open: '09:00', close: '20:00' },\n56:   },\n57: \n58:   /* ── SUPABASE (Backend) ─────────────────────────────────── */\n59:   // Sign up free at https://supabase.com → create project → Settings → API\n60:   // NEVER commit real keys to public GitHub.\n61:   // Use environment variables in production (Vercel env vars).\n62:   supabase: {\n63:     url:    typeof __SUPABASE_URL__    !== 'undefined' ? __SUPABASE_URL__    : '',\n64:     anonKey: typeof __SUPABASE_ANON__ !== 'undefined' ? __SUPABASE_ANON__   : '',\n65:     // If both are empty, the app runs in localStorage-only demo mode.\n66:   },\n67: \n68:   /* ── PAYMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n69:   payment: {\n70:     codEnabled:     true,\n71:     upiEnabled:     true,\n72:     upiId:          'yourname@upi',  // ← Replace with your UPI ID\n73:     upiName:        'Brew & Bloom Café',\n74:     // Online gateway (Razorpay / Cashfree): set keyId below.\n75:     // Leave empty to show demo-mode UPI only.\n76:     razorpayKeyId:  '',              // ← Optional: Razorpay key_id\n77:   },\n78: \n79:   /* ── ORDER TRACKING ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n80:   tracking: {\n81:     // If Supabase is not configured, demo mode kicks in automatically.\n82:     // Demo simulates a driver moving from restaurant to customer.\n83:     locationUpdateIntervalMs: 5000,  // How often driver app sends GPS (ms)\n84:     demoRouteSteps: 20,              // Steps in simulated demo route\n85:   },\n86: \n87:   /* ── MAP ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n88:   map: {\n89:     defaultZoom: 14,\n90:     // OSRM public routing API (free, no key needed)\n91:     osrmBase: 'https://router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/driving',\n92:     // Tile server (OpenStreetMap — free, no key)\n93:     tileUrl: 'https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',\n94:     tileAttribution: '© <a href=\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/\">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors',\n95:   },\n96: \n97: };\n98: \n99: // Freeze so nothing accidentally mutates config\n100: Object.freeze(CONFIG);\n101: Object.freeze(CONFIG.cafe);\n102: Object.freeze(CONFIG.restaurant);\n103: Object.freeze(CONFIG.delivery);\n104: Object.freeze(CONFIG.tax);\n105: Object.freeze(CONFIG.supabase);\n106: Object.freeze(CONFIG.payment);\n107: Object.freeze(CONFIG.tracking);\n108: Object.freeze(CONFIG.map);\n109: \n110: export default CONFIG;\n111: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:08Z","thinking":"Found a likely configuration variable for the WhatsApp number within the project's configuration file. The prompt requires this number to be easily modified by the owner, so it needs to be clearly labeled as such and set to a placeholder value, not a real number. Will ensure the example includes the country code and avoid any formatting characters like spaces or dashes.\n\n\nThe configuration file will include a clearly labeled, editable variable for the restaurant's WhatsApp number, along with validation checks in the main script to handle missing or invalid configurations, prompting a clear error message. The second requirement focuses on automatically constructing order messages that will leverage the customer's cart and checkout data to provide a well-formatted output with order details, subtotal, total, and customer information.\n\n\nConstructing the order confirmation message requires dynamically assembling information from the order snapshot. The output format must include a unique order ID, an itemized list with quantities and prices, subtotal, and delivery fee. Conditional rendering for `Home Delivery`, `Takeaway`, or `Dine-In` order types is essential.\n\nWill incorporate GST calculation (or total amount) if applicable. Customer details (name, phone, delivery address, landmark, and delivery instructions) will be included based on availability.\n\n\nRequirement three necessitates implementing a client-side WhatsApp redirection. This involves field validation, cart item check, accurate total calculation, order reference generation, dynamic message building, and URL encoding. The redirection method will leverage the `wa.me` URL format to seamlessly open the WhatsApp conversation. Requirement four emphasizes validating the order summary structure, including order type-specific details such as delivery/pickup instructions or table information, and confirming a payment method.\n\n\nImplementing changes to the main checkout button to \"Place Order on WhatsApp\" with an icon and clear explanatory text is necessary to align with the prompt. Incorporating a loading state during message preparation and preventing accidental clicks is essential for a smooth user experience.\n\nThe system will maintain user state if required fields are missing and display an error if the restaurant's WhatsApp number is not set. Building the user experience modal to clarify that the order submission occurs *after* the WhatsApp message is sent to the restaurant is critical to being honest with the customer.\n\n\nRemoved the dynamic QR code implementation based on the explicit instruction. The focus shifts towards directly integrating the WhatsApp order submission. The existing checkout flow will be replaced by the WhatsApp redirection. The UI will include a \"Place Order on WhatsApp\" button with appropriate messaging. The generated WhatsApp message needs the order reference ID.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\brew-and-bloom\\index.html","EndLine":715,"StartLine":570,"toolAction":"Reading checkout section in index.html","toolSummary":"Inspect checkout modal HTML"}}]}
