{"step_index":178,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:25Z","thinking":"The customer initiates the order process by adding items to the cart and proceeding to checkout, which opens a modal. Within the checkout modal, order type selection is the first step, presenting options like home delivery, self-pickup, and dine-in. For home delivery, the process will require location detection or address input, alongside name and mobile number entry.\n\n\nThe system requires different input fields depending on the selected order type (home delivery, takeaway, or dine-in). Home delivery necessitates address details; takeaway needs only name and mobile number, while dine-in focuses on table/seating information. The checkout process must collect the required information before proceeding to payment and order confirmation.\n\n\nWhen an \"Order on WhatsApp\" button is clicked, the system should handle different scenarios based on context; direct pre-filling for individual items, guided checkout, or direct message construction. The \"Place Order on WhatsApp\" action within the checkout modal requires rigorous field validation before generating a structured WhatsApp message, encompassing an order ID and details.\n\nThe validation encompasses a minimum cart item count, name presence, valid phone number format, and specific address information based on the order type (home delivery, takeaway, dine-in). Crucially, a configured WhatsApp number must be available for message delivery, which needs verification; otherwise, an error alert will be presented.\n\n\nThe system must format the order details for WhatsApp. It will structure the message, including itemized lists, customer details, and the order type. Different sections will appear depending on whether it's Takeaway/Self Pickup or Dine-In order.\n\nA WhatsApp redirection process will then be implemented. This includes a loading state on the button, URL encoding, constructing the WhatsApp URL, and opening WhatsApp in a new tab. A modal will display instructions for confirming and sending the order, emphasizing that the order is finalized only upon café acknowledgment.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\brew-and-bloom\\script.js","EndLine":700,"StartLine":580,"toolAction":"Reading handleOrderSubmit in script.js","toolSummary":"Inspect handleOrderSubmit implementation"}}]}
{"step_index":179,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-01T03:28:33+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-01T03:28:33+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/script.js`\nTotal Lines: 880\nTotal Bytes: 34057\nShowing lines 580 to 700\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n580:     iconAnchor: [17, 17],\n581:   });\n582: \n583:   // Default customer position ~2 km north-east in Haldia\n584:   state.customerLat = cafeLat + 0.015;\n585:   state.customerLng = cafeLng + 0.012;\n586: \n587:   state.checkoutUserMarker = L.marker([state.customerLat, state.customerLng], {\n588:     icon: userIcon,\n589:     draggable: true,\n590:   }).addTo(state.checkoutMap);\n591: \n592:   state.checkoutUserMarker.on('dragend', (e) => {\n593:     const latlng = e.target.getLatLng();\n594:     state.customerLat = latlng.lat;\n595:     state.customerLng = latlng.lng;\n596:     updateCheckoutLocation(latlng.lat, latlng.lng, 'Adjusted via map pin');\n597:   });\n598: \n599:   updateCheckoutLocation(state.customerLat, state.customerLng);\n600: }\n601: \n602: function updateCheckoutLocation(lat, lng, note = '') {\n603:   const cafeLat = CONFIG.restaurant.lat;\n604:   const cafeLng = CONFIG.restaurant.lng;\n605: \n606:   if (state.checkoutUserMarker) {\n607:     state.checkoutUserMarker.setLatLng([lat, lng]);\n608:   }\n609: \n610:   // Calculate straight-line distance\n611:   const dLat = (lat - cafeLat) * (Math.PI / 180);\n612:   const dLng = (lng - cafeLng) * (Math.PI / 180);\n613:   const a = Math.sin(dLat / 2) * Math.sin(dLat / 2) +\n614:             Math.cos(cafeLat * (Math.PI / 180)) * Math.cos(lat * (Math.PI / 180)) *\n615:             Math.sin(dLng / 2) * Math.sin(dLng / 2);\n616:   const c = 2 * Math.atan2(Math.sqrt(a), Math.sqrt(1 - a));\n617:   const straightDistanceKm = Math.round(6371 * c * 10) / 10;\n618: \n619:   // Road distance is typically ~1.25x straight line\n620:   const approxRoadDistanceKm = Math.round(straightDistanceKm * 1.25 * 10) / 10;\n621:   state.customerDistanceKm = approxRoadDistanceKm;\n622: \n623:   // Update distance badge\n624:   const distEl = document.getElementById('mapDistanceText');\n625:   const etaEl = document.getElementById('mapEtaText');\n626:   const etaMins = estimateDeliveryTime(approxRoadDistanceKm);\n627: \n628:   if (distEl) {\n629:     if (approxRoadDistanceKm > CONFIG.delivery.radiusKm) {\n630:       distEl.innerHTML = `<span style=\"color:#E74C3C;\">⚠️ Outside delivery radius (${approxRoadDistanceKm} km > ${CONFIG.delivery.radiusKm} km). Please choose Self Pickup.</span>`;\n631:     } else {\n632:       distEl.innerHTML = `🛵 Distance: <strong>${approxRoadDistanceKm} km</strong> (Approx. road route)`;\n633:     }\n634:   }\n635: \n636:   if (etaEl) {\n637:     etaEl.textContent = `Est. ETA: ~${etaMins} mins`;\n638:   }\n639: \n640:   // Draw / update straight line or route\n641:   if (state.checkoutMap) {\n642:     if (state.checkoutRouteLayer) {\n643:       state.checkoutMap.removeLayer(state.checkoutRouteLayer);\n644:     }\n645:     state.checkoutRouteLayer = L.polyline([[cafeLat, cafeLng], [lat, lng]], {\n646:       color: '#FF7629',\n647:       weight: 3,\n648:       dashArray: '6, 8',\n649:       opacity: 0.85,\n650:     }).addTo(state.checkoutMap);\n651: \n652:     state.checkoutMap.fitBounds([[cafeLat, cafeLng], [lat, lng]], { padding: [40, 40] });\n653:   }\n654: \n655:   updateCheckoutSummary();\n656: }\n657: \n658: /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n659:    ORDER SUBMISSION WORKFLOW\n660:    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */\n661: async function handleOrderSubmit(e) {\n662:   e.preventDefault();\n663: \n664:   const nameInput = document.getElementById('custName');\n665:   const phoneInput = document.getElementById('custPhone');\n666:   const addrInput = document.getElementById('custAddress');\n667:   const localInput = document.getElementById('custLocality');\n668:   const pinInput = document.getElementById('custPin');\n669:   const notesInput = document.getElementById('custNotes');\n670:   const paymentMethod = document.querySelector('input[name=\"paymentMethod\"]:checked')?.value || 'cod';\n671: \n672:   // Validation\n673:   let isValid = true;\n674: \n675:   if (!nameInput.value.trim()) {\n676:     nameInput.classList.add('invalid');\n677:     isValid = false;\n678:   } else {\n679:     nameInput.classList.remove('invalid');\n680:   }\n681: \n682:   // Indian mobile validation (10 digits starting with 6-9)\n683:   const phoneVal = phoneInput.value.trim().replace(/\\D/g, '');\n684:   if (!/^[6-9]\\d{9}$/.test(phoneVal)) {\n685:     phoneInput.classList.add('invalid');\n686:     isValid = false;\n687:   } else {\n688:     phoneInput.classList.remove('invalid');\n689:   }\n690: \n691:   if (state.deliveryMode === 'delivery') {\n692:     if (!addrInput.value.trim()) {\n693:       addrInput.classList.add('invalid');\n694:       isValid = false;\n695:     } else {\n696:       addrInput.classList.remove('invalid');\n697:     }\n698: \n699:     if (!localInput.value.trim()) {\n700:       localInput.classList.add('invalid');\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
